  "description": "High tide across Boston’s waterfront reached about 12 feet higher relative to low tide on Thursday and Friday afternoons, a phenomenon that — for now — can only occur a few times a year when the planets (literally) align. Scientists say that while this phenomenon is exceptional now, this level of flooding could become common in the coming decades if climate change continues to worsen.  Click on the link in our bio to read the story. #kingtide #bostontiktok #climatechange",
